# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only

# Configuration options for Rust BPF map implementations.
# Provides a mutually exclusive choice between C and Rust implementations
# of BPF map data structures.

choice
	prompt "BPF map implementation language"
	depends on BPF_SYSCALL
	default BPF_C_MAPS
	help
	  Select the implementation language for BPF map data structures.
	  The Rust implementation provides memory safety guarantees through
	  Rust's ownership model and type system while maintaining functional
	  equivalence with the C implementation.

config BPF_C_MAPS
	bool "C implementation (default)"
	help
	  Use the traditional C implementation of BPF map data structures.
	  This is the default and well-tested implementation.

config BPF_RUST_MAPS
	bool "Rust implementation"
	depends on RUST
	help
	  Use the Rust implementation of BPF map data structures.
	  This provides compile-time memory safety guarantees including
	  protection against use-after-free, double-free, and buffer
	  overflow vulnerabilities.

	  The Rust implementation requires the Rust toolchain (rustc) to
	  be available and CONFIG_RUST to be enabled.

	  If unsure, say N.

endchoice
